{{also|proforma}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|prō fōrmā}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-us-pro forma.oga|a=US}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-|nolinkhead=1}}

# [[occurring|Occurring]], [[undertaken]], or [[performed]] as a [[perfunctory]] matter, in the interest of [[form]], or for the [[sake]] of [[formality]].
#* {{seeCites|en}}
# Of or relating to a document of form, especially an [[invoice]] sent in advance.
# Showing projected costs, liabilities, etc., especially as a result of an expected action or situation. {{q|of a financial document}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|for the sake of form only}}
* Dutch: {{t|nl|voor de vorm}}
* Finnish: {{t|fi|muodon vuoksi}}
* French: {{t+|fr|pour la forme}}
* German: {{t+|de|pro forma}}, {{t|de|der Form wegen}}, {{t|de|der Form halber}}
* Italian: {{t|it|pro forma}}
* Japanese: {{t|ja|形式的な|tr=keishikiteki na}}
* Polish: {{t+|pl|pro forma}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-|nolinkhead=1}}

# [[undertaken|Undertaken]] or [[performed]] as a [[perfunctory]] matter, in the interest of [[form]], or for the [[sake]] of [[politeness]].
#: {{ux|en|He greeted her '''pro forma'''.}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|nolinkhead=1}}

# A [[document]] that shows the standard entries of a [[form]] or similar document.

